- defines(v1, "How was the order received?", {"via mail or phone"}): The variable range omits the "via fax" condition explicitly mentioned in the source text.
- branch(b1, XOR) / guard(b1, n5, v1 = 'via mail or phone'): The model omits the branching logic and control-flow path for when the order is "received via fax".
- action(n6, "Excel list"): The node payload represents a data artifact rather than faithfully capturing the documented source event "Once the Excel list is complete after a week".
- action(n9, "MS-Access database"): The payload represents an IT artifact/system rather than a process action.
- precedence(n18, n19): The model chronologically places the order value check (n19) after "upon receiving the actual issue" (n18), whereas the source evaluates the >5.000 € / <5.000 € condition prior to the actual issue receipt.
- precedence(n41, c3): The action "archive the memo" (n41) is modeled inside a concurrent branch before the convergence (c3). The text states "Finally, archive the memo", indicating this step should occur after the concurrent tasks have completed and joined.
- actor(a_default, ...): The model assigns all nodes to the Default actor, failing to map the explicitly responsible participant "PPC" to the action "PPC initiate production" (n26).

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR)
